 {
  "approach_name": "\"Honest linear probing behind a hopscotch-shaped facade\" — a single bin crate whose `tsl::HopscotchMap` is implemented as a power-of-two open-addressed table with linear probing, no tombstones (backward-shift erase), no neighborhood bitmaps, zero `unsafe`, and a bound-free cursor/iterator layer so the whole thing compiles in both edition 2015 (`rustc test15.rs`) and edition 2021 (`cargo build --release`).",
